    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98d5dad1_5d2b6976",
        "filename": "fastboot/1.0/IFastbootCallback.hal",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 29,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120612
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-05-17T17:42:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since only FAIL and INFO types contain descriptive messages, I made Result a struct to contain a string for the failure/info messages(the type can be determined based on the status field). The callback can hence be used strictly for messages of type INFO.\n\nstruct Result {                                                                                     \n    // status information                                                                           \n    Status status;                                                                                  \n    /**                                                                                              \n     * Log message pertaining to the status. It can be a failure message for                        \n     * Status FAILURE_UNKNOWN/NOT_SUPPORTED or an informative message for                           \n     * status SUCCESS.                                                                              \n     */                                                                                             \n    string Log;                                                                                     \n}; \n\nAlso, made the method oneway and changed the interface to IFastbootLogger.",
      "parentUuid": "26a78bbf_0ce9de28",
